+## File uploads
+
+`client.Files.Upload` (v1) takes a file name and an `io.Reader` and builds the
+multipart body for you; association targets become form fields:
+
+```go
+f, err := os.Open("report.pdf")
+if err != nil {
+	log.Fatal(err)
+}
+defer f.Close()
+
+file, err := client.Files.Upload(
+	context.Background(),
+	"report.pdf",
+	f,
+	v1.WithUploadDealID(v1.DealID(42)),
+)
+```
+
+The multipart body is buffered in memory, so uploads retry on 429/5xx like any
+other call. `Files.Add` remains available when you need full control over the
+request body; retries can only re-send a replayable body, so pass a
+`*bytes.Reader`, `*bytes.Buffer`, `*strings.Reader` or an `io.ReadSeeker`
+such as `*os.File` — any other reader fails without retrying.
+
